<title>GERMANY: Bonn offers new federal savings bond series.</title>
<headline>Bonn offers new federal savings bond series.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government offered two new series of federal savings bonds that mature on January 1 2003 and January 1 2004, the Bundesbank as issuing agent said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The yield on the type A six-year issue is 5.13 percent while the rate on the type B seven-year issue is 5.52 percent, the Bundesbank said.</p>
<p>The nominal interest rate and yield remain unchanged from the respective previous issues which mature October 1 2002 and October 1 2003.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
